///1STAT
Help by Willem Aandewiel
STAT - Disk usage, file information and attributes

///2DISKS
  E>A:STAT
  E>A:STAT E:
  E>A:STAT E:DSK:

Displays free space or disk characteristics.

///2FILES
  E>A:STAT *.HLP
  E>A:STAT DEMO.COM $S

Displays sizes, records, extents and access indicators.
CP/M uses records and allocation blocks, not exact text byte counts.

///2ATTRIBUTES
  E>A:STAT DEMO.COM $R/O
  E>A:STAT DEMO.COM $R/W

R/O makes a file read-only; R/W makes it writable again.
$SYS hides a file from the ordinary DIR display.
$DIR removes that system attribute.
These commands change the attributes of the specified files.

///2DEVICES
  E>A:STAT DEV:
  E>A:STAT VAL:
  E>A:STAT USR:

Displays device assignments, available settings or user information.
Physical device support depends on your system's BIOS.
